W: 1. As I cam' in by Turra market,
W: Turra market for to fee,
W: I fell in wi' a fairmer chiel,
W: The Barnyards of Delgaty.
W:
W:
W: (Chorus:)
W: Linten adie toorin adie,
W: Linten adie toorin ee;
W: Linten lowrin, lowrin, lowrin,
W: The Barnyards of Delgaty.
W:
W: 2. He promised me the ae best pair,
W: That ever I set my e'en upon,
W: When I gaed to the Barnyards
W: There was naething that but skin and bone.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 3. The auld black horse sat on its rump,
W: The auld white mare lay on her wime,
W: And for a' that I could 'Hup!' and crack,,
W: They wouldna rise at yokin' time.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 4. When I gae to the kirk on Sunday,
W: Mony's the bonnie lass I see,
W: Sitting by her father's side,
W: And winkin' owre the pews at me.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 5. I can drink and no' be drunk,
W: I can fecht and no' be slain,
W: I can lie wi' anither man's lass,
W: And aye be welcome to my ain.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W:
W: 6. Noo my cannie is a brunt oot,
W: My snotter's fairly on the wane,
W: Sae fare ye weel ye Barnyards,
W: Ye'll never catch me here again!
W: (Chorus:)
%
